            <ArticleTitle>Epidermoid tumour of the posterior fossa causing multiple facial pain--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 53-year-old woman presented with three types of pain. The pains had characteristics of neuralgia of the fifth cranial nerve, ninth cranial nerve, and cluster headache. On further investigation, a tumour in the posterior fossa was observed and histologically shown to be an epidermoid tumour.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
